{% extends "layout.html.twig" %}

{% block content %}
    <h1 class="title">Some Fruits freshly picked from persistence</h1>

    {# Pagination controls above #}
    {% include 'fruits/_pagination.html.twig' with { pagination: pagination } %}

    {% if pagination.results|length > 0 %}
        <div class="notification is-info is-light">
            Hint: click on a fruit to edit it!
        </div>

        <div class="columns is-multiline">
            {% for fruit in pagination.results %}
                <div class="column is-one-quarter">
                    <a href="/fruits/{{ fruit.identifier }}" class="box has-text-centered is-clickable is-block">
                        <span class="icon is-large has-text-primary mb-2">
                            <i class="fas fa-apple-alt fa-3x"></i>
                        </span>
                        <p class="title is-5 mt-2 has-text-dark">
                            {% if fruit.name %}
                                {{ fruit.name }}
                            {% else %}
                                <span class="has-text-grey-light">Nameless</span>
                            {% endif %}
                        </p>
                        <p class="subtitle is-6 has-text-grey">
                            Color: <span class="tag is-light">{{ fruit.color }}</span>
                        </p>
                    </a>
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

        {# Pagination controls below #}
        {% include 'fruits/_pagination.html.twig' with { pagination: pagination } %}

        <div class="mt-4">
            <form action="/fruits/deleteall" method="post">
                <div class="control">
                    <button class="button is-link is-warning">Delete all fruits</button>
                </div>
            </form>
        </div>
    {% else %}
        <div class="notification is-warning">
            <h3 class="title is-4">OH, WAIT! There is no Fruit yet.</h3>
            <form action="/fruits/seed" method="post">
                <div class="control">
                    <button class="button is-link is-success">Create a bunch of fruits</button>
                </div>
            </form>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="box mt-6">
        <h2 class="title is-4">Not enough fruits? Just create your own fruit here:</h2>

        <form action="/fruits/create" method="post">

            <div class="field">
                <label class="label" for="name">Name</label>
                <div class="control">
                    <input id="name" class="input" type="text" name="name">
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="field">
                <label class="label" for="color">Color</label>
                <div class="control">
                    <input id="color" class="input" type="text" name="color">
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="control">
                <button class="button is-link">Create it!</button>
            </div>
        </form>

    </div>

    <div class="content mt-6">
        <h2>The NoDB Storage</h2>

        <p>
            Since there is no configuration for any storage or database I owe you an explanation.
            BlueSprints uses the file system as storage. The full qualified class name of a model is converted into a
            directory structure. Inside the last directory all models are stored in files named by their identifier.
            The objects are serialized, since this is the fastest option to store all simple values without reflection,
            additional configuration or huge ORMs.
        </p>

        <h2>WIP !</h2>

        <p>
            The Storage function is currently work in progress. Some missing features are automatic index tables for
            searching models by their properties or the deletion of those.
        </p>

        <h2>Like it? Or not?</h2>

        <p>
            Have a look at the code which creates a fruit from the form above:
        </p>

        <pre><code class="language-php">
$arguments = $this->request->getParsedBody();
if (isset($arguments['name'], $arguments['color'])) {
    $fruit = new Fruit();
    $fruit->setColor($arguments['color']);
    $fruit->setName($arguments['name']);
    $fruit->save();
}
$this->redirect('/fruits');
        </code></pre>

        <p>
            As I promised you, it is easy as pie. If you want to alter the Model, say add a new property, just do it.
        </p>

        <p>
            <a href="/" class="button">Back to the index</a>
        </p>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
